    Lines:
      - Speaker: ""
        Text: You're from the shrine on the mountain? I've walked twelve days to leave an offering there.
      - Speaker: ""
        Text: They say the shrine bell rang by itself when the earth shook. The old songs call that a seal waking.
      - Speaker: ""
        Text: Go carefully, child. Old roads remember old things.
